• Historians estimate that cotton production in the United States rose from 3,000 bales in 1790 to 178,000 bales in 1810.', $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"Whitney's 1794 cotton gin, which could process 50 pounds of cotton daily compared to the one pound achievable by 10 hours of manual labor, represented a dramatic leap in agricultural technology."},{"key":"B","text":"Although the cotton gin is often celebrated for its processing efficiency, the device fueled a massive expansion of cotton cultivation that nearly doubled the enslaved population in cotton-producing states between 1790 and 1810, making it an engine of human bondage rather than simply a labor-saving tool."},{"key":"C","text":"Cotton production in the United States surged from 3,000 bales in 1790 to 178,000 bales in 1810, a period that coincided with the introduction and widespread adoption of Whitney's cotton gin."},{"key":"D","text":"Patented in 1794, the cotton gin mechanically separated cotton fibers from seeds at a rate 50 times faster than manual processing, transforming cotton into the dominant cash crop of the American South."}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'B', NULL, E'The correct choice is the sentence beginning "Although the cotton gin is often celebrated" because it directly challenges the labor-saving characterization by contrasting the gin''s efficiency with its role in nearly doubling the enslaved population, reframing the invention as an instrument of bondage. The sentence about the "dramatic leap in agricultural technology" reinforces the conventional view of the cotton gin as a technological achievement without addressing its social consequences. The sentence about surging cotton production presents statistics that could support either the positive or negative view without explicitly challenging the labor-saving narrative. The sentence about transforming cotton into the dominant cash crop describes the gin''s economic impact without engaging with its unintended social consequences or challenging the common characterization.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"rhetorical_purpose_error"},"B":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"rhetorical_purpose_error"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 90, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-19"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-19","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);










